18 Apr 2026 03:45:14 pm Sat

Stopped at working on the new ParseString and changing Num to use Fractions.  We're
failing on the first arithmetic x + y.  The cause was the loss of the guts of
UnitArbiter._register_unit(), which just returns the unit sent to it.  I don't know the
root cause (it could have been either of us, but clearly Mike hallucinated the single 
line "fix", as that's something a software engineer would have shouted about.

I decided on no further work, as this is stuff shouldn't be worked on when tired.  The 
next step would be to send Mike both new and old UnitArbiter code and have him inspect
to see where things changed or lost.  He should be able to fix things quickly.  My hope 
is this is the last architectural change -- and it's a big one:  new StringParser to
recognize numbers and switching to fractions.Fraction instead of two integer components.
But if we start with correct code, we should be able to recover quickly, as we've had
working self tests before.




